<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38217" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prātum</span></b> , i, n.
		(collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prātus</span></b> ,
			m., Gromat. Vet. p. 322, 5) [root prat-; Sanscr. prath,
		to spread out; cf. Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατύς,
		πλάτανος</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a meadow</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pratum irriguum, aut siccum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 8, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stercorare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrigua facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2</span></i> prooem.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pratorum viriditas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 16, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrigare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Q.
					Fr. 3, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cratire, secare, caedere, sicilire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 28, 67, § 258</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">18, 3, 4,
				§ 20</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cultus prati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 17, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">siccaneum, aut riguum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 17, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut.
			204</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Meadow-grass</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condita prata in patinis proferre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 3, 2, 22</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1,
			299</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A broad field</i>, <i>plain;</i>
			<b>poet.</b>, of the sea: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rostro Neptunia prata secare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Arat. 129</span></i>
			.</div>
